  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>beafaa0395ef12a06a81e2dddf3a5b46</srcmd5>
    <version>1.51.9</version>
    <time>1787849588</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-comfyui-frontend-package to 1.51.9.

Upstream's git tags run ahead of what is published to PyPI; Source0 is
the pythonhosted sdist, so 1.51.9 is the newest release this package
can consume (uploaded 2026-08-26, not yanked). ComfyUI upstream's own
requirements.txt now pins comfyui-frontend-package==1.51.9.

- Update to 1.51.9:
  * Render node search highlights as plain text instead of generated
    HTML, and restrict localhost downloads from the missing-model
    dialog
  * Persist workflow drafts across a page refresh, keep node preview
    images across workflow tab switches and preserve the initial node
    execution state
  * Keep Ctrl/Cmd shortcuts from falling through to the browser, add
    space-bar panning while dragging Vue nodes, and stop Canvas
    Navigation mode resetting to Custom on reload
  * Resolve widget labels, output names and tooltips from the backend
  * Cut minimap change-detection cost on large graphs, and harden the
    VIDEO_EDIT widget and its filmstrip generation
  * Tolerate a missing /api/i18n endpoint and an unusable localStorage
    during bootstrap
  * Replace lobe-i18n with an in-house locale pipeline and repair
    stale and malformed locale data
  * Lift Select and SearchAutocomplete dropdowns above modal dialogs;
    a malformed MatchType spec no longer deletes the input
  * Default an active templates search to Popular instead of Relevance
  * Route all error reports through a single reporter, which adds a
    bundled Datadog browser SDK chunk (Apache-2.0) that this build
    never initialises
  * Assorted node-editor, Cloud billing, workspace and asset fixes -
    see upstream's release notes for the full list


No patches are carried. Upstream ships no dependency change: setup.py,
setup.cfg, MANIFEST.in and __init__.py are byte-identical to 1.50.6,
install_requires stays empty and requires-python stays &gt;= 3.9.
openSUSE:Factory/comfyui requires this package with a floor
(&gt;= 1.50.6), so the bump does not affect its resolvability.

The new vendor-datadog chunk is the Apache-2.0 Datadog browser SDK.
Its only init call site sits behind a __DISTRIBUTION__ === 'cloud'
branch that is dead-code-eliminated from this build, so nothing in
the shipped assets can initialise it.

Built locally for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: succeeded, rpmlint 0
errors 0 warnings 0 badness (unchanged vs the 1.50.6 baseline);
source_validator rc 0.</comment>
    <requestid>1373925</requestid>
